    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 1 Redford Park is a well-appointed three-bedroom detached bungalow enjoying a prominent position near the entrance to this mature and highly sought-after residential development on the northern side of Greystones. Offering well-proportioned single-storey accommodation, this home is complemented by a spacious rear garden and a detached garden cabin offering further versatility and convenience. Noting that this home would benefit from modernisation, there is excellent potential for a new owner to further enhance or extend the property, subject to the necessary planning permission. This presents potential purchasers with a wonderful opportunity to acquire a home that they can transform and tailor to their own tastes and requirements.\n\nAccessed through an entrance porch, the hallway provides a natural flow from the reception rooms to the bedrooms. To the front, the living room is a bright and welcoming formal reception space, where a large picture window overlooks the front garden, and an open fireplace with granite surround provides a central focal point. The kitchen/dining room is positioned to the rear and enjoys a pleasant outlook over the garden, fitted with a range of eye and floor-level units and offering space for family dining. The rear garden can be accessed from the side door through the kitchen. \nThere are three bedrooms arranged off the central hallway. The first bedroom is a well-proportioned double room to the front with built-in wardrobes, while the second and third bedrooms are positioned to the rear. Bedroom three opens directly into a light-filled sunroom, a charming additional reception space surrounded by glazing and overlooking the garden. A family bathroom completes the internal accommodation.\n\nOutside, the spacious rear garden is enclosed by timber fencing and enhanced by a selection of mature trees, offering an excellent canvas for gardening, outdoor dining or future development, subject to planning permission. A side passage provides convenient pedestrian access to the front, where the garden is laid partly in lawn and incorporates a driveway providing off-street parking. An excellent feature of this home is the generous detached garden room, which is supplied with electricity and wired for an alarm. Currently laid out as a home office with a separate adjoining store, this versatile space is ideally suited to hybrid working but could equally serve as a den, studio, or gym.\n\nRedford Park is a mature and well-established residential development, featuring generous green spaces and enjoying a convenient position within easy reach of Greystones town centre. The nearby Blacklion area offers a choice of shops, schools and leisure amenities, while the town centre provides an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, boutiques and everyday services. Greystones is also renowned for its coastal lifestyle, with beaches, scenic walks, the harbour and marina all readily accessible. Transport connections are well catered for, with local bus services and Greystones DART station providing convenient access to Dublin, while the N11/M11/M50 road network is also within easy reach. A wide variety of sporting and recreational amenities can be enjoyed locally, including golf, sailing, rugby, tennis, GAA and the facilities at Shoreline Leisure Centre."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 2.47m x 5.14m\nAccessed via porch, leads to;\n\nLiving Room - 3.37m x 4.48m\nFormal reception room overlooking front garden through large picture window. Open fireplace with granite surrounding inset.\n\nBedroom 1 - 2.67m x 3.27m\nDouble room to front with built-in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.56m x 3.05m\nTo rear with built-in wardrobes.\n\nBathroom - 1.68m x 1.82m\nWC, wash-hand basin, bath with showerhead attachment.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.47m x 3.05m\nTo rear, leading to;\n\nSun Room / Conservatory - 2.93m x 2.99m\nLight filled sunroom overlooking rear garden.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 3.37m x 4.72m\nOverlooking rear garden, eye and floor level units, provision for oven and hob. Stainless steel sink unit.\n\nGarden Room - 3.45m x 2.43m\nSpacious detached garden room to rear with electricity and wiring for alarm. Perfect for home office or den. Includes separate outdoor storage space.\n\n"
      },
      {
